# AI agent manager

One command for local AI coding-agent hygiene and the open Agent Skills
ecosystem. The registry covers Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI,
Qwen Code, OpenCode, Kilo, Cline, Aider, goose, Vibe, Amp, Cursor, Kiro,
Droid, OpenHands, Pi, and Rovo Dev. Market discovery delegates to the open
`skills` CLI, whose live compatibility table supports more than 70 agents
without duplicating that fast-changing catalog here.

## Actions

### `doctor`

Finds installed executables, runs version checks, validates JSON/TOML settings,
checks state-directory permissions, and locates the agent's skill directory.
Select `--fix` to preview owner-only permission repairs and missing skill
directories; applying does not install agents or rewrite their settings.

### `clean`

Use `--kind sessions`, `--kind memories`, `--kind cache`, or `--kind all`.
Only documented local state is targeted. Credentials, API keys, configuration,
skills, plugins, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, and equivalent
project-authored instructions are excluded.

Close affected agents before applying. Copilot and Amp can sync state to a
service; deleting local files does not delete remote copies.

### `market`

Enter a `--query` to search interactively. To preview an install, set
`--install owner/repository`, optionally `--skill name`, choose an `--agent`,
and select `--global` for user scope. Apply only after reviewing the source:
skills can bundle executable scripts.

## Direct CLI

```sh
agent doctor --list-agents
agent doctor --agent codex --fix
agent clean sessions --agent claude-code
agent clean all --agent codex --apply
agent market "Python security"
agent market --install vercel-labs/agent-skills --skill find-skills --agent codex
```

Without `--apply`, destructive and repair commands only print their plan.
Direct applies require typing `APPLY`; the shared TUI performs its own `CLEAN`
confirmation and then supplies `--apply --yes`.

See `docs/agent-tools.md` for researched storage, diagnostics, market
compatibility, and limitations.
